      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To find the altitude of a triangle, we can use the formula for the area of a triangle, which is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{altitude} \\]\n\nWe are given that the area of the triangle is 600 square feet and the length of the corresponding base is 30 feet. We need to find the altitude. Let's denote the altitude by \\( h \\). Substituting the given values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[ 600 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 30 \\times h \\]\n\nTo isolate \\( h \\), we first multiply both sides of the equation by 2:\n\n\\[ 1200 = 30 \\times h \\]\n\nNext, we divide both sides by 30:\n\n\\[ h = \\frac{1200}{30} = 40 \\]\n\nTherefore, the altitude of the triangle is \\(\\boxed{40}\\) feet.",
